00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:43.370
Miyako

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:48.340
Miyako
I believed that we would win
if we worked together.

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:48.610
Yuno

00:12:48.610 --> 00:12:54.550
Yuno
All of you were supporting me,
so I didn't want to waste your efforts.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:56.310
Yuno
The baton was really heavy!

00:12:56.650 --> 00:13:01.320
All for one, and one for all.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:05.400
We were losing, but we weren't falling behind.

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:09.300
No one seemed to be giving up,
so I thought we could do it.

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:16.140
I didn't think I cared whether we won
or lost, but now that we won...

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:17.440
It feels good, doesn't it?

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:19.240
Health Room

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.070
Wake up, Ms. Yoshinoya.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:27.020
Why are you resting and not
helping to clean up?

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:31.590
Because I'm tired. I can't move anymore.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:36.650
You pervert!

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:43.430
I wasn't able to help Red Team very much.

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:45.030
That's not true.

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:50.600
In the scavenger hunt, I was distracted by
a dog and during pushball...

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.210
Sorry, sorry.

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:56.810
I just remembered what happened.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:59.210
You really stirred up the crowd.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:01.480
Everyone screamed and ran away.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:06.520
I couldn't see where I was going,
so I went off course.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.350
You really charged right in.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.090
You too, Miya-chan.

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:13.320
You rode on top of the ball.
You surprised me.

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:17.370
But I didn't break any rules.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.490
I rolled the ball to the finish line.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.810
Still, you're not a circus clown.

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:25.070
What was surprising was
the mock cavalry battle.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:27.310
That?

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:28.500
Tent Tent Tent Tent Tent
Parents Parents
Parents Western Army Eastern Army Parents
Parents Parents

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:35.180
I'll give fifty bonus points to the
team that steals my headband.

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:39.920
Now's my chance to defeat the
principal fair and square.

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:40.890
Thud

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:43.960
Prepare yourself!

00:14:57.210 --> 00:15:01.410
If we had those bonus points, we would
have been able to beat the Pink Team.

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:05.410
Well, Ms. Yoshinoya gave it her all.

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:08.240
We won against White, so things are fine.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:11.850
We haven't won against the White Team
for quite some time, have we?

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:15.330
We apparently haven't won against
them for five years.

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:19.530
We might continue to beat
them while we're here.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:21.360
We're lucky if we do.

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:26.500
I was able to participate this year
and Miyako was also a big help.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.870
She got a lot of points in
the first-year events.

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:31.740
Thank you, thank you.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:36.410
Sae was amazing too. She was the
one who rallied everyone.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:39.050
I suppose I did what I could.

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:42.020
You earned lots of points too, Hiro.

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:45.020
Really? I was just absorbed
in what I was doing.

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:46.620
Was that any good?

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:49.560
Yunocchi did her part in the whole team relay.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:52.000
Huh? I didn't do much.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.330
All of you built up a lead for me.

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:55.630
Not at all.

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:59.030
If you hadn't run the way you did,
the White Team wouldn't have lost.

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:01.130
You ran well, Yunocchi!

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:05.070
Thank you, Miya-chan.

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:08.410
But Natsume looked frustrated.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.310
It was just a three point difference.

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:17.750
Natsume...

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:22.460
Even if it's just three points, a win is a win.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:26.300
Well, I'll let you enjoy your victory for today.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:29.560
Field day is just for fun after all.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:33.020
I'm not frustrated at all!

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:40.210
Never mind Natsume.

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:42.370
I don't understand her anyway.

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:48.150
Hiro, we're out of snacks.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:51.450
Miya-chan, what time do you eat dinner?

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:53.580
You mustn't overeat.

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.030
Then, give me dinner.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.390
Hey...

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.990
I've got a lot of ingredients left
over from the packed lunch.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:03.530
If you don't mind me making
something from that...

00:17:03.530 --> 00:17:06.900
I won't be picky. I will eat it up!

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.600
Sae and Yuno too.

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:09.670
Is it all right?

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.570
Thank you.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:16.680
The radish is delicious!

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.250
The enoki is also delicious!

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:20.780
Dinner is also completely white.

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:23.120
The same goes for my breakfast.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:28.460
That usually happens whenever you pack
lunches for field trips, doesn't it?

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:29.460
That's right.

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:31.160
You can usually tell what you're
going to have in your packed lunch

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:32.790
by what you had for breakfast.

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:35.100
Can I turn on the TV?

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:37.230
Is there a show you want to watch? What is it?

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:39.470
How does it feel to be to be back, Chocolat?

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:41.530
That's Lovely Chocolat, isn't it?

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:45.230
Yeah, it's back for a two hour special.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.900
Oh?

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:48.780
Oh, it's my house!

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:52.010
Chocolat, there's something
I have to tell you first.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:55.390
What's this? There's a family
of strangers in here.

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:59.010
The furniture is different and
even the wallpaper is new!

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:02.190
This is a big mystery, Chocoyama-kun!

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:05.630
This is a big mystery, Chokoyama-kun.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:08.060
Wow, it hasn't changed at all.

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:09.100
Yeah...

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.300
You're right.

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:12.670
But Chocolat sure has aged.

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:15.370
You think so too?

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:17.230
Me too.

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:20.740
She's a little too old to be wearing that.

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:23.750
Actually, I think so too.

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:26.010
How old is this actor?

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.280
Chokoyama-kun, huh?

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:30.750
He's a little too old for "kun."

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:33.060
Yeah, I think he's a "san."

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:36.820
And we're watching this even
though we're in high school.

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:40.050
Getting older really sucks.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:43.460
Hiro what time did you wake up today?

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:46.900
It must have been early,
since you packed a lunch.

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:48.870
It was one hour earlier than usual.

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:52.800
About that time, I heard footsteps
going down the stairs.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:55.340
I could tell that it was Miya-chan going out.

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:57.510
Miya-chan, did you wake up that early?

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:00.580
My meeting time was moved to an earlier time.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:03.140
We couldn't prepare the day before.

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:06.490
Oh yeah, the rain stopped over night.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:12.050
When we met up this morning,
we set up tents and planted flags.

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:14.960
It must have been tough being part
of the executive committee.

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.330
Good work.

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:19.200
It was a lot of fun, including the accidents.

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:23.040
Did you notice that the
announcements were hijacked?

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:24.370
The runner who got passed the baton just now is
Red Team's Sae of second year.
Since her body has few curves, she is able to
run with little wind resistance!

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:26.110
That Yosshi...

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:29.980
Before that, it was taken over by the
broadcasting club's president.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:31.250
Huh?

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:33.310
That was supposed to be the job
of the executive committee!

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:39.620
I'm Toudou of Third Year, the president of
Yamabuki High School's broadcasting club.

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:42.720
Allow me to make the announcements.

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:44.890
Time to begin vocal exercises!

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.660
But we had a lot of fun.

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:52.170
I was really excited by the
situation at the end.

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.040
The whole team relay, huh?

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:56.110
You ran well, Yunocchi.

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:57.200
Thank you.

00:19:57.470 --> 00:20:00.040
I had a great time.

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:02.780
The Yamabuki Festival is coming up soon.

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:04.150
Really?

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:06.480
I still haven't decided what I'm going to do!

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:09.650
Thinking about it makes me nervous.

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:10.880
I hope we'll be all right.

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:14.660
Is your class doing something?

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:16.820
We're probably doing a play.

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:20.430
Our class is also thinking of doing a play.

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:22.560
I'd like to do a restaurant.

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:27.070
No use thinking about it today. I can't think.

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:28.630
We're pretty worn out after all.

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:34.270
Oh, is this a new product?

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:35.510
Wow!

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:38.540
It's shining. Oh, it burst.

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:41.340
Didn't we see this before?

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:43.210
We did! Around spring!

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:45.950
We didn't get around to eating it.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.960
It didn't go on sale.

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:49.530
It looks delicious.

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:51.490
Let's look for it again.

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:55.570
That was delicious!

00:20:55.570 --> 00:20:57.360
I'm glad you enjoyed it.

00:20:57.800 --> 00:20:58.940
Now then!

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:01.630
Oh, I'll help you clean up.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:04.110
What should I do?

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:05.880
Perhaps I should put it off until tomorrow.

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:07.210
Why don't you do that.

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:09.940
Take a bath and go to sleep for today.

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:13.380
I'll pass on that as well.

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:16.750
I took a shower as soon as I got home.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.410
Why not? You'll be able to sleep well.

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:25.190
Don't worry about me.
I'm able to sleep already.

00:21:25.190 --> 00:21:28.290
I won't wake up until morning.

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:31.230
Miyako, let's go back to our rooms.

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:33.800
You ran well, Yunocchi!

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:36.570
Huh? You can stop saying that!

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:43.110
No peeking!

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:51.020
I feel better already.

00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:56.990
I'm glad I tried my best.

00:21:58.060 --> 00:22:04.970
Thrash and pulverize!

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:09.770
October 13 The End
Boing
